        "original_id": "b51bfa5f-4da6-5ba0-ae07-83278e098685",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lower Lake Stone Jail, Sulphur Bank Mine\n- Industries: quicksilver and mercury mining\n- Topics: town growth, civil order, jail construction\n\nFacts:\n- From 1873 to 1883, the first quicksilver operations of the Sulphur Bank Mine drove rapid town growth and created an urgent need for civil order.\n- During that 1873 to 1883 period, the need for civil order led to the building of the Lower Lake Stone Jail.\n- The Sulphur Bank Mine covered 150 acres and became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2d4e3e56-a40f-57b5-9a09-fce746609c6d",
        "text": "Page: Lower Lake Stone Jail. Sentence: During the days of the first quicksilver operations of the Sulphur Bank Mine, lasting from 1873 to 1883, rapid town growth and the urgent need for civil order necessitated the building of a jail.\nPage: Sulphur Bank Mine. Sentence: The 150 acre mine became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world.",
